This module provides the coroutine scheduling primitives used to execute
asynchronous Mint coroutines.

A {Runtime.Scheduler} is used to spawn coroutines and coordinate their execution.
A spawned coroutine can suspend by providing an {Runtime.Operation}, allowing it
to wait asynchronously until the operation completes. Once the operation
completes, the scheduler resumes the suspended coroutine.

Spawning a coroutine produces a {Runtime.Promise} representing its eventual
completion. The promise can be used to determine whether the coroutine has
completed and to retrieve its result.

The module provides three core abstractions:
* {Runtime.Scheduler} schedules and executes coroutines.
* {Runtime.Operation} represents an asynchronous operation on which a coroutine can suspend.
* {Runtime.Promise} represents the completion and result of a spawned coroutine.

```mn
let scheduler = Runtime.Scheduler()

let promise = scheduler.spawn(def [...]() {
    return await scheduler.suspend(MyOperation())
})

scheduler.run()

let result = promise.get()
```
